.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payouts - Send a wallet's tokens to your own venue (lists when run bare; requires login)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payouts [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Pay out: move a merchant wallet's tokens to a deposit address at a venue of your
own — an exchange account, Circle Mint, another wallet you control. Run bare to
list the account's payouts.

.PP
The gateway does the on-chain leg and nothing else. It builds an unsigned ERC-20
transfer from the wallet to a registered destination; this CLI checks it is
EXACTLY that transfer (token, recipient, amount, chain, no value) and signs it
locally with your key. The gateway never holds funds or keys and never talks to
the venue.

.PP
First payout to a new venue:
  1. payouts destinations add -c  -t USDC -A 0xDeposit… --min-amount 
       register the deposit address; you confirm you checked the details
  2. payouts send --destination  --proof -p @merchant-key
       a small proof transfer (1 token unit, raised to the minimum)
  3. payouts destinations confirm 
       once the venue shows the proof CREDITED: the destination is verified
  4. payouts send --destination  --amount 250.00 -p @merchant-key
       or --amount all: the balance minus the refund reserve

.PP
Minimum: a deposit below the venue's minimum may be ignored by the venue and lost
for good. Every destination states it (--min-amount, or --no-minimum when the venue
has none): payouts below it are refused.

.PP
Refund reserve: '--amount all' keeps the destination's reserve in the wallet, so
refunds still inside their window can be paid (default: the gateway's suggestion,
the refundable balance of the wallet's payments in that token).

.PP
A payout goes pending → submitted → confirmed (or failed: its error_code says
why). One pending payout per destination. A deactivated account is read-only: it
cannot prepare, send or change payouts or destinations (403 account_deactivated).

.PP
Every read covers the whole account; writes act for the wallet you sign in with,
which must be the destination's.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--created-from\fP=""
	Only payouts created at/after this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB--created-to\fP=""
	Only payouts created at/before this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB--destination\fP=""
	Only payouts to this destination (destination id)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for payouts

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Payouts per page (max 100)

.PP
\fB--purpose\fP=""
	Filter by purpose: payout or proof

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort fields (e.g. -created_at)

.PP
\fB--status\fP=[]
	Filter by status (pending, submitted, confirmed, failed); repeat or comma-separate for any of several

.PP
\fB--wallet\fP=""
	Only payouts from this wallet (wallet id)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payouts
  rail0 payouts --status submitted,confirmed --purpose payout
  rail0 payouts send --destination <destination_id> --amount 100.00 -p @merchant-key
  rail0 payouts get <payout_id>
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0(1)\fP, \fBrail0-payouts-cancel(1)\fP, \fBrail0-payouts-destinations(1)\fP, \fBrail0-payouts-events(1)\fP, \fBrail0-payouts-get(1)\fP, \fBrail0-payouts-list(1)\fP, \fBrail0-payouts-prepare(1)\fP, \fBrail0-payouts-report-hash(1)\fP, \fBrail0-payouts-resend(1)\fP, \fBrail0-payouts-send(1)\fP, \fBrail0-payouts-submit(1)\fP
